### Shell Execution Rules
- Do not chain commands with `&&`, `;`, or `|` (including `|| true`) when individual tool calls can be made.
- Do not use command substitutions like `$(cmd)`. Run the inner command first, then use the literal result.
- Avoid wrappers (`sudo`, `eval`, `bash <script>`, or `PATH=...` prefixes). Call allowlisted scripts and binaries directly by bare name (e.g. `open-pr.sh`, `pr-body.sh`, `workflow-manifest.sh`) so commands remain auto-approvable.
- Use `grep -rn` instead of `rg` (`rg` is not installed).
- Write temporary/scratch files (including PR body drafts and commit message files) under `<worktree>/.scratch/` rather than `/tmp`.

